    {
      "id": "checklist",
      "audioPath": "video-production/understanding-contrasts/audio/checklist.m4a",
      "audioSeconds": 44.990204,
      "durationSeconds": 45.840204,
      "durationInFrames": 1376,
      "startSeconds": 299.452313,
      "startFrame": 8986
    }
  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "A first-level model can contain several explanatory variables, but a scientific result usually begins with a narrower question.",
      "startSeconds": 0,
      "endSeconds": 7.8337295604395605,
      "startFrame": 0,
      "endFrame": 236
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "Was the response during left-button trials greater than the response during right-button trials?",
      "startSeconds": 7.8337295604395605,
      "endSeconds": 13.491423131868132,
      "startFrame": 235,
      "endFrame": 405
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "Was one condition positively related to the measured BOLD signal?",
      "startSeconds": 13.491423131868132,
      "endSeconds": 17.84349510989011,
      "startFrame": 404,
      "endFrame": 536
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "A contrast turns a question like that into a precise set of weights.",
      "startSeconds": 17.84349510989011,
      "endSeconds": 23.50118868131868,
      "startFrame": 535,
      "endFrame": 706
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "In this lesson, we will connect those weights to the parameter estimates in the general linear model, interpret baseline and difference contrasts, and identify the quality-control checks that prevent a correct calculation from answering the wrong question.",
      "startSeconds": 23.50118868131868,
      "endSeconds": 39.603854999999996,
      "startFrame": 705,
      "endFrame": 1189
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "At each voxel, FEAT fits the general linear model.",
      "startSeconds": 40.453855000000004,
      "endSeconds": 44.4885443,
      "startFrame": 1213,
      "endFrame": 1335
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "text": "The design matrix contains the explanatory variables, or EVs, and beta contains one estimated coefficient for each model column.",
      "startSeconds": 44.4885443,
      "endSeconds": 53.00622171111111,
      "startFrame": 1334,
      "endFrame": 1591
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "text": "Those coefficients describe how strongly each predictor contributes to the observed signal after accounting for the other predictors.",
      "startSeconds": 53.00622171111112,
      "endSeconds": 61.07560031111112,
      "startFrame": 1590,
      "endFrame": 1833
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "text": "A contrast does not refit the model and does not change the original beta estimates.",
      "startSeconds": 61.07560031111112,
      "endSeconds": 67.80008247777778,
      "startFrame": 1832,
      "endFrame": 2035
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "text": "Instead, it defines a linear combination of selected estimates.",
      "startSeconds": 67.80008247777778,
      "endSeconds": 71.83477177777777,
      "startFrame": 2034,
      "endFrame": 2156
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "text": "In compact notation, the contrast estimate is c transpose beta.",
      "startSeconds": 71.83477177777779,
      "endSeconds": 76.3177598888889,
      "startFrame": 2155,
      "endFrame": 2290
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "text": "The vector c contains the weights that encode the hypothesis.",
      "startSeconds": 76.3177598888889,
      "endSeconds": 80.80074800000001,
      "startFrame": 2289,
      "endFrame": 2425
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "text": "Suppose the original EV order is Left followed by Right.",
      "startSeconds": 81.65074800000001,
      "endSeconds": 85.75860565217393,
      "startFrame": 2449,
      "endFrame": 2573
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "text": "The contrast one, zero selects the Left coefficient.",
      "startSeconds": 85.75860565217393,
      "endSeconds": 89.04489177391305,
      "startFrame": 2572,
      "endFrame": 2672
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "text": "In the usual FEAT task model, it tests a positive Left effect relative to the implicit baseline represented by the rest of the model.",
      "startSeconds": 89.04489177391305,
      "endSeconds": 98.90375013913044,
      "startFrame": 2671,
      "endFrame": 2968
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "text": "Zero, one selects the Right coefficient.",
      "startSeconds": 98.90375013913044,
      "endSeconds": 101.36846473043478,
      "startFrame": 2967,
      "endFrame": 3042
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "text": "These are not direct comparisons between Left and Right.",
      "startSeconds": 101.3684647304348,
      "endSeconds": 105.06553661739132,
      "startFrame": 3041,
      "endFrame": 3152
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "text": "They ask whether each selected estimate is positive in its modeled context.",
      "startSeconds": 105.06553661739132,
      "endSeconds": 109.99496580000002,
      "startFrame": 3151,
      "endFrame": 3300
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "text": "A contrast using one, one tests the positive sum of the two coefficients.",
      "startSeconds": 109.99496580000002,
      "endSeconds": 115.3351807478261,
      "startFrame": 3299,
      "endFrame": 3461
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "text": "Using one half, one half gives their numerical average.",
      "startSeconds": 115.3351807478261,
      "endSeconds": 119.03225263478262,
      "startFrame": 3460,
      "endFrame": 3571
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "text": "Those scaled contrasts have the same t or z statistic, but their cope values are on different scales, so name and report them carefully.",
      "startSeconds": 119.03225263478262,
      "endSeconds": 128.89111100000002,
      "startFrame": 3570,
      "endFrame": 3867
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "text": "To compare Left directly with Right, use one, negative one.",
      "startSeconds": 129.74111100000002,
      "endSeconds": 134.03294773913046,
      "startFrame": 3892,
      "endFrame": 4021
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "text": "This computes beta Left minus beta Right.",
      "startSeconds": 134.03294773913046,
      "endSeconds": 137.03723345652176,
      "startFrame": 4020,
      "endFrame": 4112
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "text": "The null hypothesis is that the weighted difference equals zero, and the positive direction tests whether Left is greater than Right.",
      "startSeconds": 137.03723345652176,
      "endSeconds": 146.05009060869568,
      "startFrame": 4111,
      "endFrame": 4382
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "text": "Reversing the signs gives negative one, one, which tests Right greater than Left.",
      "startSeconds": 146.05009060869565,
      "endSeconds": 151.62947836956522,
      "startFrame": 4381,
      "endFrame": 4549
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "text": "A negative weight does not mean deactivation.",
      "startSeconds": 151.62947836956522,
      "endSeconds": 154.63376408695652,
      "startFrame": 4548,
      "endFrame": 4640
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "text": "It means that the corresponding coefficient is subtracted in this particular hypothesis.",
      "startSeconds": 154.63376408695655,
      "endSeconds": 159.78396817391308,
      "startFrame": 4639,
      "endFrame": 4794
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "text": "Direction matters: Left greater than Right and Right greater than Left are related, but they are not interchangeable labels for one contrast.",
      "startSeconds": 159.78396817391305,
      "endSeconds": 169.226009,
      "startFrame": 4793,
      "endFrame": 5077
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "text": "Contrast numbers only have meaning when they are aligned with the correct design-matrix columns.",
      "startSeconds": 170.07600900000003,
      "endSeconds": 176.18753891489365,
      "startFrame": 5102,
      "endFrame": 5286
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "text": "If the actual order is Right then Left, the weights one, negative one test Right greater than Left, even if the contrast is named Left greater than Right.",
      "startSeconds": 176.18753891489365,
      "endSeconds": 188.4105987446809,
      "startFrame": 5285,
      "endFrame": 5653
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "text": "Before running FEAT, write the EV order, read each contrast as a sentence, and point from every weight to its displayed column name.",
      "startSeconds": 188.41059874468087,
      "endSeconds": 198.45096931914895,
      "startFrame": 5652,
      "endFrame": 5954
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "text": "Then inspect the design preview.",
      "startSeconds": 198.45096931914895,
      "endSeconds": 200.63365857446811,
      "startFrame": 5953,
      "endFrame": 6020
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "text": "Empty columns, swapped timing files, duplicated predictors, or unexpected derivatives can all change the interpretation.",
      "startSeconds": 200.63365857446811,
      "endSeconds": 207.18172634042557,
      "startFrame": 6019,
      "endFrame": 6216
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "text": "A plausible activation map cannot repair a mislabeled hypothesis.",
      "startSeconds": 207.18172634042554,
      "endSeconds": 211.110567,
      "startFrame": 6215,
      "endFrame": 6334
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "text": "In FEAT, open Full model setup and then Contrasts and F-tests.",
      "startSeconds": 211.96056700000003,
      "endSeconds": 216.65240920879123,
      "startFrame": 6358,
      "endFrame": 6500
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "text": "Give each contrast a scientific name rather than a generic number.",
      "startSeconds": 216.65240920879123,
      "endSeconds": 221.34425141758243,
      "startFrame": 6499,
      "endFrame": 6641
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "text": "Enter the weights in the displayed EV order.",
      "startSeconds": 221.34425141758246,
      "endSeconds": 224.75650029670334,
      "startFrame": 6640,
      "endFrame": 6743
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "text": "For the source lab, the model contains Left and Right EVs, followed by contrasts for each condition, both directional differences, and a combined positive effect.",
      "startSeconds": 224.75650029670334,
      "endSeconds": 235.4197780439561,
      "startFrame": 6742,
      "endFrame": 7063
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "text": "The screenshot here is evidence from the real teaching workflow, not a generated interface.",
      "startSeconds": 235.41977804395606,
      "endSeconds": 241.3912135824176,
      "startFrame": 7062,
      "endFrame": 7242
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "text": "Before selecting Done, compare every row with the approved analysis plan and save the design file so the model specification remains reproducible.",
      "startSeconds": 241.3912135824176,
      "endSeconds": 250.77489800000004,
      "startFrame": 7241,
      "endFrame": 7524
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "text": "For each contrast, FEAT writes several related outputs.",
      "startSeconds": 251.62489800000003,
      "endSeconds": 255.45978902040818,
      "startFrame": 7548,
      "endFrame": 7664
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "text": "The cope is the contrast of parameter estimates: the weighted effect in the units of the model.",
      "startSeconds": 255.45978902040818,
      "endSeconds": 263.6089324387755,
      "startFrame": 7663,
      "endFrame": 7909
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "text": "The varcope describes uncertainty in that contrast estimate.",
      "startSeconds": 263.6089324387755,
      "endSeconds": 267.4438234591837,
      "startFrame": 7908,
      "endFrame": 8024
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "text": "Dividing the cope by its standard error produces a t statistic, which FEAT converts to a z statistic for inference and reporting.",
      "startSeconds": 267.4438234591837,
      "endSeconds": 277.98977376530615,
      "startFrame": 8023,
      "endFrame": 8340
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "text": "A z-statistic map is therefore standardized evidence, not an effect-size map.",
      "startSeconds": 277.98977376530615,
      "endSeconds": 283.2627489183674,
      "startFrame": 8339,
      "endFrame": 8498
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "text": "Higher-level analyses use the cope together with its varcope.",
      "startSeconds": 283.2627489183674,
      "endSeconds": 287.5770013163266,
      "startFrame": 8497,
      "endFrame": 8628
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "text": "Thresholded z-statistic images help visualize inferential results, but interpretation should begin only after checking preprocessing, registration, the design matrix, and the contrast definition.",
      "startSeconds": 287.5770013163266,
      "endSeconds": 298.60231300000004,
      "startFrame": 8627,
      "endFrame": 8959
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "text": "Before you run FEAT, complete five checks.",
      "startSeconds": 299.452313,
      "endSeconds": 302.73284870833334,
      "startFrame": 8983,
      "endFrame": 9082
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "text": "First, list EVs in matrix order.",
      "startSeconds": 302.73284870833334,
      "endSeconds": 305.5447364583333,
      "startFrame": 9081,
      "endFrame": 9167
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "text": "Second, state the scientific question for every contrast.",
      "startSeconds": 305.5447364583333,
      "endSeconds": 309.293920125,
      "startFrame": 9166,
      "endFrame": 9279
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "text": "Third, translate the sentence into weights and then translate the weights back into a sentence.",
      "startSeconds": 309.293920125,
      "endSeconds": 316.3236395,
      "startFrame": 9278,
      "endFrame": 9490
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "text": "Fourth, inspect the design matrix and contrast arrows visually.",
      "startSeconds": 316.3236395,
      "endSeconds": 320.541471125,
      "startFrame": 9489,
      "endFrame": 9617
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "text": "Fifth, distinguish the effect estimate, its uncertainty, and the standardized statistic you will later report.",
      "startSeconds": 320.541471125,
      "endSeconds": 327.5711905,
      "startFrame": 9616,
      "endFrame": 9828
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "text": "If the design, weights, and scientific language tell the same story, the contrast is ready to run.",
      "startSeconds": 327.5711905,
      "endSeconds": 335.53820579166666,
      "startFrame": 9827,
      "endFrame": 10067
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "text": "Next, the hands-on walkthrough will configure these contrasts in a live Neurodesk session and inspect the corresponding FEAT outputs.",
      "startSeconds": 335.53820579166666,
      "endSeconds": 344.442517,
      "startFrame": 10066,
      "endFrame": 10334
    }
  ]
}
